                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I always appreciate indie projects. [i]GudeAndi[/i] says himself that this was a project for him that he completed after work and under the circumstances not much time could be devoted to it. The story is about us getting stuck on floor 7 and our job is to escape. We interact with our surroundings, solve some puzzles and experience a couple of jump-scares.\n\nVoice acting is great - I do not believe an English version is necessary since the subtitles help. The issue I had with the game was the lack of optimisation. When you hit ESC you can see some gfx settings but it isn't much. With some more time this could have been fine-tuned. At this point there is screen tearing and I also got inconsistent FPS values.\n\nStill, as the store page says this is a fun project and it has some scary parts. If you are fine with checking out such games instead of just playing AAA titles then [i]Stockwrk7[/i] is for you. After all, it is completely free of charge and it is a short horror walking sim.",
